---
import UtilityLayout from "../../layouts/UtilityLayout.astro";
import ExtraUtilityApp from "../../components/ExtraUtilityApp.astro";
---

<UtilityLayout
  title="Ask a webpage"
  description="Ask about a public page or pasted text. Get the exact supporting passage."
  slug="ask-a-webpage"
>
  <ExtraUtilityApp tool="qa" />
  <details class="prose tool-help">
    <summary>How this tool works &amp; limits</summary>
    <h2>What this tool does</h2>
    <p>
      This tool returns exact supporting paragraphs, not a generated essay. Jev
      checks answer presence separately from selecting a passage. Unsupported
      questions return not answered; partial evidence is labeled. Pasted text
      can come from any source. Public HTTP/HTTPS hostname URLs are supported,
      including bare hostnames (HTTPS by default). Every redirect repeats URL
      and DNS safety checks. The reader executes no scripts or embedded
      requests. Logins, paywalls, access blocks, JavaScript-only content, PDFs
      and large pages may require pasted text. UTF-8 HTML/plain text is limited
      to 250,000 bytes, eight seconds and three redirects; only the first 10,000
      characters and 100 paragraphs are searched, with truncation disclosed.
    </p>
    <h2>Privacy and uncertainty</h2>
    <p>
      Only explicit AI requests send bounded source context to Jev through our
      protected server. There is no account or application input-history
      database. AI classifications can be wrong; typed output is not proof of
      truth. <a href="/privacy/">Read privacy and operating limits.</a>
    </p>
  </details>
</UtilityLayout>
